Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] x86/mm/pat: Flush all TLBs for scattered CPA ranges

cpa_flush() flushes the range starting at the first address for
cpa->numpages pages.  With CPA_ARRAY and CPA_PAGES_ARRAY the addresses
are not contiguous, so the other pages keep their old TLB entries.  The
INVLPGB flush hides this today because it ignores the address, but the
IPI-based flush already misses them, and so will INVLPGB once it honours
the address.

Flush everything for the array modes.  Upstream reverted the whole
optimization instead (a39a7014825b), going back to IPIs for every small
flush.
---
--- a/arch/x86/mm/pat/set_memory.c
+++ b/arch/x86/mm/pat/set_memory.c
@@ -447,7 +447,7 @@ static void cpa_flush(struct cpa_data *cpa, int cache)
 
 	start = fix_addr(__cpa_addr(cpa, 0));
 	end =   start + cpa->numpages * PAGE_SIZE;
-	if (cpa->force_flush_all)
+	if (cpa->force_flush_all || cpa->flags & (CPA_ARRAY | CPA_PAGES_ARRAY))
 		end = TLB_FLUSH_ALL;
 
 	flush_tlb_kernel_range(start, end);
